# Local request examples. Use a client that keeps response cookies between requests.
# Set real credentials locally; demo account instructions are in server/README.md.
# Replace every UUID/hash/token placeholder before running the related request.
# Login: run CSRF bootstrap, copy URL-decoded XSRF-TOKEN cookie into xsrfToken, then login.
# Mutations may rotate the cookie: keep xsrfToken synchronized with the latest cookie.
# Business requests use browser/session cookies; runtime requests use the separate tool JWT.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@runtimeOrigin = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@frontendOrigin = http://localhost:3000
@email = you@example.test
@password = SET_YOUR_LOCAL_PASSWORD
@xsrfToken = COPY_URL_DECODED_XSRF_COOKIE
@institutionId = REPLACE_WITH_INSTITUTION_UUID
@subjectId = REPLACE_WITH_SUBJECT_UUID
@termId = REPLACE_WITH_TERM_UUID
@offeringId = REPLACE_WITH_OFFERING_UUID
@assessmentId = REPLACE_WITH_ASSESSMENT_UUID
@roleId = REPLACE_WITH_ROLE_UUID
@roleAssignmentId = REPLACE_WITH_OWN_ROLE_ASSIGNMENT_UUID
@userId = REPLACE_WITH_TARGET_USER_UUID
@applicationId = REPLACE_WITH_REQUEST_UUID
@groupId = REPLACE_WITH_GROUP_UUID
@attemptId = REPLACE_WITH_ATTEMPT_UUID
@markId = REPLACE_WITH_MARK_UUID
@workspaceId = REPLACE_WITH_WORKSPACE_UUID
@documentId = REPLACE_WITH_DOCUMENT_UUID
@contentHash = REPLACE_WITH_LATEST_CONTENT_HASH
@toolId = REPLACE_WITH_TOOL_UUID
@versionId = REPLACE_WITH_TOOL_VERSION_UUID
@workSessionId = REPLACE_WITH_RECORDED_WORK_SESSION_UUID
@runtimeToken = REPLACE_WITH_TOOL_JWT
@scopeCode = REPLACE_WITH_ONE_TIME_CODE

### Database/schema readiness (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health
Accept: application/json

### 1. Bootstrap session/XSRF cookies
GET {{baseUrl}}/sanctum/csrf-cookie
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### 2. Login; client must send the cookies from the preceding response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"email":"{{email}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### 3. Get own identity/contexts and copy IDs from response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Directory is available to a signed-in user without a role assignment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institution-directory?search=Example&perPage=15
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Role eligibility for onboarding
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/requestable-roles
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### System admin: create institution
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/institutions
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"name":"Example University","website":"https://example.edu"}

### Institution subject manager: create subject
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/subjects
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"subjectCode":"COMP1000","subjectName":"Programming","subjectDescription":"Introduction to programming"}

### Create term and its teaching period
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/terms
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"year":2027,"session":1,"periods":[{"name":"Teaching","type":"TEACHING","startAt":"2027-02-15T00:00:00Z","endAt":"2027-05-17T00:00:00Z"}]}

### Open the subject in the term; both IDs must belong to this institution
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/offerings
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"subjectId":"{{subjectId}}","termId":"{{termId}}"}

### Published individual assessment; create/activate the tool separately first
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/offerings/{{offeringId}}/assessments
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"name":"Assignment 1","weight":25,"isGroup":false,"publishAt":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z","dueAt":"2027-03-15T12:00:00Z","allowedToolIds":["{{toolId}}"]}

### Permission catalog for role editor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/permissions
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Create offering-scoped student role (requires institution role.create/delegation authority)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/roles
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"roleCode":"offering:student","roleName":"Student","scopeType":"OFFERING","requestMode":"PUBLIC","permissions":["offering.view","assessment.view_published","assessment.attempt","attempt.view_own","tool.launch","tool_session.replay_own"]}

### Grant role and offering scope to a user (run with appropriate grant/delegation authority)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/role-assignments
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"userId":"{{userId}}","roleId":"{{roleId}}","offeringIds":["{{offeringId}}"]}

### Scoped manager list omits every other offering's scopes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/role-assignments?offeringId={{offeringId}}&perPage=20
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Student: request role identity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/role-requests
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"roleId":"{{roleId}}","note":"Please grant access."}

### Reviewer: process that request once
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/role-requests/{{applicationId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"decision":"APPROVED","note":"Enrollment checked."}

### Student: request offering scope for own active OFFERING role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/scope-requests
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"roleAssignmentId":"{{roleAssignmentId}}","offeringId":"{{offeringId}}"}

### Alternatively redeem a code supplied by an authorized issuer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/scope-codes/redeem
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"code":"{{scopeCode}}","roleAssignmentId":"{{roleAssignmentId}}"}

### Student offerings in one selected context; omit query to use the union of applicable roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/offerings?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Published assessment and tools
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/assessments/{{assessmentId}}?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### For group assessments only: create group (student creator is included automatically)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/assessments/{{assessmentId}}/groups?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"name":"Team A","memberIds":["{{userId}}"]}

### Start individual attempt; for group assessment add groupId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/attempts?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"assessmentId":"{{assessmentId}}"}

### Workspace includes folder entries/tools; copy workspaceId from attempt response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Create source file; response contains documentId/contentHash
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/documents
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"name":"main.py","entryKind":"FILE","parentFolderId":null,"content":"print('hello')\n"}

### Read bytes and current ETag (this is not a JSON metadata endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/documents/{{documentId}}/content
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/octet-stream

### Save RAW bytes with the current content hash; missing header=428, stale hash=412
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/documents/{{documentId}}/content
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}
If-Match: "{{contentHash}}"

print('updated')

### Launch assessment work tool from PLATFORM origin, then open response.runtimeUrl in a new tab
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tool/v1/sessions
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"mode":"WORK","attemptId":"{{attemptId}}","toolId":"{{toolId}}","roleAssignmentId":"{{roleAssignmentId}}"}

### Inside tool: use TOOL JWT (not account PAT/session token)
GET {{runtimeOrigin}}/api/tool/v1/context
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{runtimeToken}}

### Recording checkpoint, before scheduling the next batch
GET {{runtimeOrigin}}/api/tool/v1/events/checkpoint
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{runtimeToken}}

### Event batch; replace batchId with fresh UUID once, preserve it and exact payload for retries
POST {{runtimeOrigin}}/api/tool/v1/events
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{runtimeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"batchId":"REPLACE_WITH_CLIENT_BATCH_UUID","seqStart":0,"seqEnd":0,"clientAt":"2027-03-01T01:00:00.000Z","events":[{"type":"file.open","documentId":"{{documentId}}"}]}

### Refresh BEFORE 300-second tool token expires
POST {{runtimeOrigin}}/api/tool/v1/token
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{runtimeToken}}

### Close recording owner session
PATCH {{runtimeOrigin}}/api/tool/v1/session
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{runtimeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Submit student attempt; file/event writes will now be forbidden
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/attempts/{{attemptId}}/submit?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{}

### Teacher: get marking detail and recorded session IDs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/attempts/{{attemptId}}?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Teacher: create/continue own draft (submitted attempt required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/attempts/{{attemptId}}/marks?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{}

### Teacher: edit draft
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/attempts/{{attemptId}}/marks/{{markId}}?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"score":82.5,"outOf":100,"feedback":"Good explanation."}

### Teacher: submit draft revision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/attempts/{{attemptId}}/marks/{{markId}}/submit?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{}

### Explicit official result selection (attempt.result.finalize permission)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/institutions/{{institutionId}}/attempts/{{attemptId}}/result?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"markId":"{{markId}}","note":"Final result."}

### Replay launch uses tool's CURRENT active version; recorded session still pins its original version
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tool/v1/sessions
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"mode":"REPLAY","workSessionId":"{{workSessionId}}","roleAssignmentId":"{{roleAssignmentId}}"}

### Read recorded batches using the NEW replay JWT from the previous response
GET {{runtimeOrigin}}/api/tool/v1/replay/sessions/{{workSessionId}}/events?afterSeq=-1&limit=100
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{runtimeToken}}

### Private date-only plan (no UTC conversion)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/assessment-plans/{{assessmentId}}?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"startDate":"2027-03-01","endDate":"2027-03-07"}

### Aggregate calendar
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/calendar?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### Private timed event requires explicit timezone
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/calendar-events?roleAssignmentId={{roleAssignmentId}}
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"title":"Study session","startAt":"2027-03-01T08:00:00+11:00","endAt":"2027-03-01T10:00:00+11:00","offeringId":"{{offeringId}}"}

### Authenticated active tool catalog (ordinary users cannot inspect inactive versions)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tools
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json

### System admin: create tool metadata; ZIP upload is a separate multipart request in API reference
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/tools
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{"code":"example-editor","name":"Example Editor","description":"Practice tool"}

### Activate an uploaded immutable version (system admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/tools/{{toolId}}/versions/{{versionId}}/activate
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{}

### Upload tool version ZIP (system admin)
# Create server/tool.zip with tool.json at ZIP root, then run this request.
# The HTTP client reads the local binary file; the server never reads a client-side path string.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/tools/{{toolId}}/versions
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LernumiExampleBoundary

--LernumiExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="package"; filename="tool.zip"
Content-Type: application/zip

< ./tool.zip
--LernumiExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="releaseNotes"

Initial package version
--LernumiExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="activate"

1
--LernumiExampleBoundary--

### Logout current browser session; GET auth/session should then return 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{}
